(   strictly) Tj
T*
(   inside the cone, the body remains statically stable; if R lies on the conical surface, motion) Tj
T*
(   impends.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Mathematical Proof that Angle of Repose Equals Angle of Friction \(theta_r = phi_s\):) Tj
T*
(   Consider a block of weight W resting on a rough plane inclined at angle theta to the) Tj
T*
(   horizontal.) Tj
T*
(   Resolve the gravitational body weight W into orthogonal components:) Tj
T*
(   W_parallel = W * sin\(theta\) \(acting down the plane, driving shear motion\)) Tj
T*
(   W_perpendicular = W * cos\(theta\) \(acting normal to the plane, compressing surfaces\)) Tj
T*
(   From equilibrium perpendicular to the incline:) Tj
T*
(   Sigma F_perp = 0 => N - W * cos\(theta\) = 0 => N = W * cos\(theta\)) Tj
T*
(   From equilibrium along the incline at impending downward slip \(theta = theta_r\):) Tj
T*
(   Sigma F_parallel = 0 => W * sin\(theta_r\) - F_lim = 0 => F_lim = W * sin\(theta_r\)) Tj
T*
(   By Coulomb's friction law, F_lim = mu_s * N. Substituting for F_lim and N:) Tj
T*
(   W * sin\(theta_r\) = mu_s * [ W * cos\(theta_r\) ]) Tj
T*
(   Dividing both sides by W * cos\(theta_r\):) Tj
T*
(   sin\(theta_r\) / cos\(theta_r\) = mu_s => tan\(theta_r\) = mu_s) Tj
T*
(   Since by definition tan\(phi_s\) = mu_s, it follows directly that:) Tj
T*
(   tan\(theta_r\) = tan\(phi_s\) => theta_r = phi_s.) Tj
T*
(   Thus, the angle of repose is proved to be identically equal to the angle of limiting friction.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
