(>> Solution to Question 3:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: A 500 N block rests on a rough horizontal surface with mu_s = 0.35 and mu_k = 0.30. A pulling force P inclined at 25 degrees above the horizontal is applied to the block. Calculate the magnitude of P required to \(1\) initiate sliding, \(2\) maintain uniform steady motion once moving.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Problem Parameters and Free Body Diagram \(FBD\):) Tj
T*
(   Weight of block: W = 500 N acting vertically downwards.) Tj
T*
(   Inclination of pulling force P: theta = 25 degrees above the horizontal.) Tj
T*
(   Coefficients of friction: mu_s = 0.35 \(static\), mu_k = 0.30 \(kinetic\).) Tj
T*
(   Forces acting on the block:) Tj
T*
(   - Downward gravity weight: W = 500 N.) Tj
T*
(   - Upward normal reaction from floor: N.) Tj
T*
(   - Pulling force components: P_x = P * cos\(25 deg\), P_y = P * sin\(25 deg\) \(upward\).) Tj
T*
(   - Tangential frictional resistance F directed horizontally opposing motion.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Vertical Equilibrium Equation \(Sigma Fy = 0\):) Tj
T*
(   N + P * sin\(25 deg\) - W = 0) Tj
T*
(   N = 500 - P * sin\(25 deg\) = 500 - 0.4226 * P.) Tj
T*
(   Note that the upward vertical component of P relieves contact pressure and reduces N!) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Case 1: Minimum Force P_init to Initiate Motion \(Impending Slip\):) Tj
T*
(   At impending motion, friction reaches limiting static friction: F = F_lim = mu_s * N.) Tj
T*
(   Horizontal equilibrium \(Sigma Fx = 0\):) Tj
T*
(   P * cos\(25 deg\) - mu_s * N = 0) Tj
T*
(   P * cos\(25 deg\) - 0.35 * [ 500 - P * sin\(25 deg\) ] = 0) Tj
T*
(   0.9063 * P - 175.0 + 0.35 * 0.4226 * P = 0) Tj
T*
(   0.9063 * P + 0.1479 * P = 175.0) Tj
T*
(   1.0542 * P = 175.0) Tj
T*
(   P_init = 175.0 / 1.0542 = 166.00 N.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Case 2: Force P_maintain to Maintain Steady Motion \(Dynamic Equilibrium\):) Tj
T*
(   During ongoing motion with constant velocity \(a = 0\), friction is kinetic: F = F_k = mu_k * N.) Tj
T*
ET

