BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: A uniform ladder AB of length L = 6 m and weight W = 300 N rests against a rough vertical wall at B \(mu_w = 0.25\) with its lower end A on a rough horizontal floor \(mu_f = 0.35\). Determine the minimum angle of inclination theta with the horizontal for stable static equilibrium.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Free Body Diagram of Ladder AB at Impending Slip:) Tj
T*
(   - Length: L = 6.0 m; Weight W = 300 N acting at midspan G \(L/2 = 3.0 m\).) Tj
T*
(   - Base A \(Floor\): Contact normal reaction N_A acts vertically upward.) Tj
T*
(   Since ladder tends to slip outward to the left, friction F_A acts to the right: F_A = mu_f *) Tj
T*
(   N_A = 0.35 * N_A.) Tj
T*
(   - Top B \(Wall\): Contact normal reaction N_B acts horizontally to the left.) Tj
T*
(   Since top B tends to slide downward, friction F_B acts vertically upward: F_B = mu_w * N_B =) Tj
T*
(   0.25 * N_B.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Force Equilibrium Equations at Impending Motion:) Tj
T*
(   \(a\) Horizontal Equilibrium \(Sigma Fx = 0\):) Tj
T*
(   F_A - N_B = 0 => N_B = F_A = 0.35 * N_A.) Tj
T*
(   \(b\) Vertical Equilibrium \(Sigma Fy = 0\):) Tj
T*
(   N_A + F_B - W = 0) Tj
T*
(   Since F_B = 0.25 * N_B, substitute N_B = 0.35 * N_A:) Tj
T*
(   N_A + 0.25 * \(0.35 * N_A\) = 300) Tj
T*
(   N_A * \(1 + 0.0875\) = 300) Tj
T*
(   1.0875 * N_A = 300 => N_A = 275.86 N.) Tj
T*
(   \(c\) Contact Forces:) Tj
T*
(   N_B = 0.35 * 275.86 = 96.55 N.) Tj
T*
(   F_A = 96.55 N, F_B = 0.25 * 96.55 = 24.14 N.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Moment Equilibrium about Base A \(Sigma M_A = 0, CCW +\):) Tj
T*
(   Taking moments of all forces about contact point A:) Tj
T*
(   - Clockwise moment of self-weight W:) Tj
T*
(   M_W = - W * \(L/2\) * cos\(theta\) = - 300 * 3.0 * cos\(theta\) = - 900 * cos\(theta\)) Tj
T*
(   - Counterclockwise moment of normal wall reaction N_B:) Tj
T*
(   M_NB = + N_B * L * sin\(theta\) = + 96.55 * 6.0 * sin\(theta\) = + 579.3 * sin\(theta\)) Tj
T*
(   - Counterclockwise moment of wall friction F_B:) Tj
T*
(   M_FB = + F_B * L * cos\(theta\) = + 24.14 * 6.0 * cos\(theta\) = + 144.84 * cos\(theta\)) Tj
T*
(   Setting sum of moments to zero:) Tj
T*
(   579.3 * sin\(theta\) + 144.84 * cos\(theta\) - 900 * cos\(theta\) = 0) Tj
T*
(   579.3 * sin\(theta\) = \(900 - 144.84\) * cos\(theta\)) Tj
T*
(   579.3 * sin\(theta\) = 755.16 * cos\(theta\)) Tj
T*
(   tan\(theta\) = 755.16 / 579.3 = 1.3036) Tj
T*
(   theta = atan\(1.3036\) = 52.51 degrees.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Conclusion:) Tj
T*
(   The minimum safe angle of inclination with the floor to prevent slipping is theta = 52.51) Tj
T*
ET

