(   Angle of friction: phi = atan\(mu\) = atan\(0.25\) = 14.04 degrees.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Analysis of the Vertical Load Block:) Tj
T*
(   Forces acting on the raised block:) Tj
T*
(   - Downward load: W = 20 kN.) Tj
T*
(   - Horizontal reaction from smooth vertical guide: R_guide.) Tj
T*
(   - Total contact reaction R1 from inclined face of the wedge.) Tj
T*
(   Since the wedge moves horizontally to the right, the block slides up the wedge incline.) Tj
T*
(   Therefore, reaction R1 is inclined at \(alpha + phi\) to the vertical:) Tj
T*
(   theta_1 = alpha + phi = 15.0 deg + 14.04 deg = 29.04 degrees to the vertical.) Tj
T*
(   Applying vertical equilibrium to the block \(Sigma Fy = 0\):) Tj
T*
(   R1 * cos\(alpha + phi\) - W = 0) Tj
T*
(   R1 * cos\(29.04 deg\) = 20 kN) Tj
T*
(   R1 = 20 / cos\(29.04 deg\) = 20 / 0.8743 = 22.88 kN.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Analysis of the Horizontal Wedge:) Tj
T*
(   Forces acting on the driving wedge:) Tj
T*
(   - Horizontal driving force: P directed to the right.) Tj
T*
(   - Normal and friction reaction from bottom floor: R2.) Tj
T*
(   Since wedge moves right, friction on floor acts to the left.) Tj
T*
(   Hence, reaction R2 is inclined at angle phi = 14.04 deg to the vertical.) Tj
T*
(   - Action force from load block: R1 = 22.88 kN acting downward and left at 29.04 deg to) Tj
T*
(   vertical.) Tj
T*
(   Applying horizontal and vertical equilibrium to the wedge:) Tj
T*
(   Sigma Fy = 0 => R2 * cos\(phi\) - R1 * cos\(alpha + phi\) = 0) Tj
T*
(   R2 * cos\(14.04 deg\) = 22.88 * cos\(29.04 deg\) = 20.0 kN) Tj
T*
(   R2 = 20.0 / cos\(14.04 deg\) = 20.0 / 0.9701 = 20.62 kN.) Tj
T*
(   Applying horizontal equilibrium \(Sigma Fx = 0\):) Tj
T*
(   P - R2 * sin\(phi\) - R1 * sin\(alpha + phi\) = 0) Tj
T*
(   P = [ 20.62 * sin\(14.04 deg\) ] + [ 22.88 * sin\(29.04 deg\) ]) Tj
T*
(   P = \(20.62 * 0.2425\) + \(22.88 * 0.4854\) = 5.00 + 11.11 = 16.11 kN.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Conclusion:) Tj
T*
(   The horizontal driving effort required to raise the 20 kN foundation load is P = 16.11 kN.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
