BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: A square-threaded screw jack has a mean diameter d_m = 50 mm and pitch p = 10 mm. The coefficient of thread friction is mu = 0.15. If a load of W = 25 kN is to be raised, calculate: \(1\) Helix angle, \(2\) Tangential effort at mean diameter, \(3\) Torque required, \(4\) Efficiency, \(5\) Check whether the screw is self-locking.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Calculation of Geometric Parameters & Friction Angle:) Tj
T*
(   Mean diameter: d_m = 50 mm = 0.050 m; Mean radius: r_m = 25 mm = 0.025 m.) Tj
T*
(   Pitch: p = 10 mm = 0.010 m.) Tj
T*
(   Lead angle alpha:) Tj
T*
(   tan\(alpha\) = p / \(pi * d_m\) = 10 / \(pi * 50\) = 10 / 157.08 = 0.06366) Tj
T*
(   alpha = atan\(0.06366\) = 3.64 degrees.) Tj
T*
(   Friction angle phi:) Tj
T*
(   tan\(phi\) = mu = 0.15 => phi = atan\(0.15\) = 8.53 degrees.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Tangential Effort to Raise Load \(P\):) Tj
T*
(   Tangential effort applied at mean thread radius:) Tj
T*
(   P = W * tan\(alpha + phi\)) Tj
T*
(   alpha + phi = 3.64 deg + 8.53 deg = 12.17 degrees.) Tj
T*
(   tan\(12.17 deg\) = 0.2157) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
