BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: A flat belt drive transmits power between two pulleys. The angle of wrap on the smaller pulley is theta = 160 degrees and mu = 0.30. If the maximum permissible belt tension is 2.5 kN, determine the maximum power that can be transmitted at a belt speed of 15 m/s \(neglecting centrifugal tension\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Conversion of Contact Angle to Radians:) Tj
T*
(   Wrap angle: theta = 160 degrees.) Tj
T*
(   theta_rad = 160 * \(pi / 180\) = 2.7925 radians.) Tj
T*
(   Friction coefficient: mu = 0.30.) Tj
T*
(   Belt speed: v = 15.0 m/s.) Tj
T*
(   Maximum tight-side tension: T1 = 2.5 kN = 2500 N.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Determination of Slack Side Tension \(T2\):) Tj
T*
(   Applying the Capstan belt friction equation:) Tj
T*
(   T1 / T2 = exp\(mu * theta\)) Tj
T*
(   mu * theta = 0.30 * 2.7925 = 0.83775) Tj
T*
(   exp\(0.83775\) = 2.3112) Tj
T*
(   T1 / T2 = 2.3112) Tj
T*
(   T2 = T1 / 2.3112 = 2500 / 2.3112 = 1081.69 N.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Net Effective Driving Force \(T_eff\):) Tj
T*
(   T_eff = T1 - T2 = 2500 - 1081.69 = 1418.31 N = 1.418 kN.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Calculation of Power Transmitted:) Tj
T*
(   Power P = \(T1 - T2\) * v) Tj
T*
(   Power P = 1418.31 N * 15.0 m/s = 21,274.65 Watts = 21.27 kW.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   5. Conclusion:) Tj
T*
(   The maximum power deliverable by the flat belt without slipping is 21.27 kW.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
