(   [Problem Statement]: Two blocks A \(weight 200 N\) and B \(weight 300 N\) are connected by a light inextensible cord passing over a smooth pulley. Block A rests on a horizontal plane \(mu = 0.25\) and block B rests on a 30-degree incline \(mu = 0.20\). Determine the acceleration of the system and cable tension.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. System Free Body Diagrams and Direction of Motion:) Tj
T*
(   Let us test for motion down the incline:) Tj
T*
(   Component of weight of B down incline: W_B * sin\(30 deg\) = 300 * 0.50 = 150 N.) Tj
T*
(   Maximum static friction on B: F_B_max = mu_B * W_B * cos\(30 deg\) = 0.20 * 300 * 0.866 = 51.96) Tj
T*
(   N.) Tj
T*
(   Maximum static friction on A: F_A_max = mu_A * W_A = 0.25 * 200 = 50.0 N.) Tj
T*
(   Total resisting friction = 51.96 + 50.0 = 101.96 N.) Tj
T*
(   Since driving gravity force \(150 N\) > total resistance \(101.96 N\), the system accelerates with) Tj
T*
(   B moving down!) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Dynamic Equations of Motion \(Newton's Second Law Sigma F = m*a\):) Tj
T*
(   Mass of A: m_A = 200 / 9.81 = 20.39 kg.) Tj
T*
(   Mass of B: m_B = 300 / 9.81 = 30.58 kg.) Tj
T*
(   Kinetic friction on A: F_kA = 0.25 * 200 = 50.0 N.) Tj
T*
(   Kinetic friction on B \(acting up the incline\): F_kB = 0.20 * 300 * cos\(30 deg\) = 51.96 N.) Tj
T*
(   \(a\) For Block A \(moving horizontally to the right\):) Tj
T*
(   T - F_kA = m_A * a) Tj
T*
(   T - 50.0 = 20.39 * a ===> [Equation 1]) Tj
T*
(   \(b\) For Block B \(moving down the 30 deg incline\):) Tj
T*
(   W_B * sin\(30 deg\) - T - F_kB = m_B * a) Tj
T*
(   150.0 - T - 51.96 = 30.58 * a) Tj
T*
(   98.04 - T = 30.58 * a ===> [Equation 2]) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Simultaneous Solution for Acceleration \(a\) and Tension \(T\):) Tj
T*
(   Add Equation 1 and Equation 2 to eliminate T:) Tj
T*
ET

