BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Derive the centrifugal tension expression T_c = m*v^2 in a moving belt and prove that maximum power occurs when T_c = T_max / 3.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Problem Context & Governing Principles:) Tj
T*
(   This problem investigates the limiting equilibrium and friction mechanics for civil engineering) Tj
T*
(   applications.) Tj
T*
(   Governing criteria involve Coulomb's dry friction law, non-concurrent moment equilibrium,) Tj
T*
(   and normal/tangential coordinate projections at contacting interfaces.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Mathematical Formulation & Step-by-Step Analysis:) Tj
T*
(   Centrifugal Tension and Maximum Power in Belt Drives:) Tj
T*
(   1. Centrifugal Force on an Infinitesimal Belt Element:) Tj
T*
(   Consider a belt element of mass dm = m * R * d\(theta\) rotating at speed v around pulley radius) Tj
T*
(   R:) Tj
T*
(   Centrifugal force dF_c = dm * \(v^2 / R\) = \(m * R * d\(theta\)\) * \(v^2 / R\) = m * v^2 * d\(theta\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Radial Balance:) Tj
T*
(   2 * T_c * sin\(d\(theta\)/2\) = dF_c => 2 * T_c * \(d\(theta\)/2\) = m * v^2 * d\(theta\) => T_c = m *) Tj
T*
(   v^2.) Tj
T*
(   3. Maximum Power Proof:) Tj
T*
(   Power P = \(T1 - T2\) * v = T1 * [ 1 - exp\(-mu*theta\) ] * v.) Tj
T*
(   Total tight side tension cannot exceed T_max: T_max = T1 + T_c => T1 = T_max - m*v^2.) Tj
T*
(   P = \( T_max - m*v^2 \) * C * v = C * \( T_max * v - m * v^3 \).) Tj
T*
(   For maximum power, dP/dv = 0:) Tj
T*
(   T_max - 3 * m * v^2 = 0 => T_max = 3 * T_c => T_c = T_max / 3. \(Proved\)) Tj
T*
(   Optimal velocity: v_opt = sqrt\( T_max / \(3 * m\) \).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Detailed Physical Verification & Equilibrium Check:) Tj
T*
(   - Normal contact forces must satisfy Sigma F_n = 0 across all boundary contact interfaces.) Tj
T*
(   - Frictional forces must not exceed limiting value F <= mu * N for stable static equilibrium.) Tj
T*
(   - Moment balance Sigma M = 0 ensures no rotational tipping or rocking instability occurs.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Civil & Structural Engineering Implications:) Tj
T*
(   In foundation retaining walls, dam bases, and structural bolted connections, an adequate) Tj
T*
(   factor of safety \(FS >= 1.5\) against sliding is mandatory under severe seismic and wind loads.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
