(   Mechanics of Rolling Resistance:) Tj
T*
(   1. Microscopic Asymmetry:) Tj
T*
(   When a hard cylinder or wheel rolls over a deformable ground plane under normal load W, the) Tj
T*
(   contact surface indents. Due to internal material hysteresis and elastic recovery lag, the) Tj
T*
(   pressure distribution is non-symmetric, shifting forward by distance c_r.) Tj
T*
(   2. Moment Equilibrium:) Tj
T*
(   The resultant normal ground reaction N = W is shifted forward by distance c_r from the wheel) Tj
T*
(   center line.) Tj
T*
(   To maintain steady rolling at constant velocity, driving horizontal force F_r applied at center) Tj
T*
(   O must overcome the restoring couple:) Tj
T*
(   F_r * R = W * c_r => F_r = \( c_r / R \) * W.) Tj
T*
(   3. Coefficient of Rolling Resistance:) Tj
T*
(   c_r has units of length \(mm or m\), representing the forward shift of normal reaction.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Detailed Physical Verification & Equilibrium Check:) Tj
T*
(   - Normal contact forces must satisfy Sigma F_n = 0 across all boundary contact interfaces.) Tj
T*
(   - Frictional forces must not exceed limiting value F <= mu * N for stable static equilibrium.) Tj
T*
(   - Moment balance Sigma M = 0 ensures no rotational tipping or rocking instability occurs.) Tj
