/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Derive the torque transmitted by a truncated conical pivot bearing under the uniform pressure and uniform wear assumptions.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Problem Context & Governing Principles:) Tj
T*
(   This problem investigates the limiting equilibrium and friction mechanics for civil engineering) Tj
T*
(   applications.) Tj
T*
(   Governing criteria involve Coulomb's dry friction law, non-concurrent moment equilibrium,) Tj
T*
(   and normal/tangential coordinate projections at contacting interfaces.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Mathematical Formulation & Step-by-Step Analysis:) Tj
T*
(   Conical Pivot Bearing Torque Derivation:) Tj
T*
(   Let cone semi-apex angle be alpha, inner radius r1, outer radius r2, axial thrust W, friction) Tj
T*
(   mu.) Tj
T*
(   1. Uniform Pressure Theory \(New Bearings\):) Tj
T*
(   Pressure p = W / [ pi * \(r2^2 - r1^2\) ].) Tj
T*
(   T = \(2/3\) * \(mu * W / sin\(alpha\)\) * [ \(r2^3 - r1^3\) / \(r2^2 - r1^2\) ].) Tj
T*
(   2. Uniform Wear Theory \(Worn-in Bearings\):) Tj
T*
(   Wear p * r = C.) Tj
T*
(   T = 0.5 * \(mu * W / sin\(alpha\)\) * \(r1 + r2\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Detailed Physical Verification & Equilibrium Check:) Tj
T*
(   - Normal contact forces must satisfy Sigma F_n = 0 across all boundary contact interfaces.) Tj
T*
