(   V-Belt Wedge Action and Power Capacity:) Tj
T*
(   1. Groove Wedging Mechanics:) Tj
T*
(   A V-belt fits into a pulley groove of included angle 2*beta \(groove semi-angle beta approx 18) Tj
T*
(   deg\).) Tj
T*
(   Radial force equilibrium: 2 * R_N * sin\(beta\) = dN => R_N = dN / \(2 * sin\(beta\)\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Enhanced Frictional Resistance:) Tj
T*
(   Total friction dF = 2 * mu * R_N = 2 * mu * [ dN / \(2 * sin\(beta\)\) ] = [ mu / sin\(beta\) ] * dN.) Tj
T*
(   Effective friction coefficient: mu_prime = mu / sin\(beta\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Power Comparison:) Tj
T*
(   Since beta approx 18-20 deg, sin\(beta\) approx 0.31-0.34, making mu_prime approx 3 * mu!) Tj
T*
(   The tension ratio T1/T2 = exp\(mu_prime * theta\) increases dramatically, generating vastly) Tj
T*
(   larger \(T1 - T2\) and power without slipping.) Tj
T*
() Tj
