/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: A screw jack with pitch 8 mm and mean diameter 40 mm lowers a 15 kN load. mu = 0.15. Calculate the torque to lower.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Problem Context & Governing Principles:) Tj
T*
(   This problem investigates the limiting equilibrium and friction mechanics for civil engineering) Tj
T*
(   applications.) Tj
T*
(   Governing criteria involve Coulomb's dry friction law, non-concurrent moment equilibrium,) Tj
T*
(   and normal/tangential coordinate projections at contacting interfaces.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Mathematical Formulation & Step-by-Step Analysis:) Tj
T*
(   Torque to Lower Load:) Tj
T*
(   tan\(alpha\) = 8 / \(pi * 40\) = 0.06366 => alpha = 3.64 deg.) Tj
T*
(   tan\(phi\) = 0.15 => phi = 8.53 deg.) Tj
T*
(   Since phi > alpha \(8.53 > 3.64\), the screw is self-locking.) Tj
T*
(   Effort to lower: P = W * tan\(phi - alpha\) = 15000 * tan\(8.53 - 3.64\) = 15000 * tan\(4.89 deg\) =) Tj
T*
(   15000 * 0.08555 = 1283.2 N.) Tj
T*
(   Torque T = P * \(d_m / 2\) = 1283.2 * 0.02 = 25.66 N*m.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Detailed Physical Verification & Equilibrium Check:) Tj
T*
