(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the stick-slip friction phenomenon and its engineering implications in machine tool slideways and earthquakes.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Problem Context & Governing Principles:) Tj
T*
(   This problem investigates the limiting equilibrium and friction mechanics for civil engineering) Tj
T*
(   applications.) Tj
T*
(   Governing criteria involve Coulomb's dry friction law, non-concurrent moment equilibrium,) Tj
T*
(   and normal/tangential coordinate projections at contacting interfaces.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Mathematical Formulation & Step-by-Step Analysis:) Tj
T*
(   Stick-Slip Oscillation Mechanics:) Tj
T*
(   1. Mechanism: Arises from the disparity between static friction \(mu_s\) and kinetic friction) Tj
T*
(   \(mu_k < mu_s\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Cycle: The driving system elastically deforms \(stick phase\) until force reaches F_lim. Once) Tj
T*
(   sliding initiates, friction drops to F_k, accelerating the mass \(slip phase\) until it stops and) Tj
T*
(   resticks.) Tj
T*
(   3. Implications: Causes squealing of railway brakes, chattering in machine tool machining, and) Tj
T*
(   forms the fundamental mechanical model for tectonic earthquake fault ruptures.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Detailed Physical Verification & Equilibrium Check:) Tj
T*
(   - Normal contact forces must satisfy Sigma F_n = 0 across all boundary contact interfaces.) Tj
T*
(   - Frictional forces must not exceed limiting value F <= mu * N for stable static equilibrium.) Tj
T*
(   - Moment balance Sigma M = 0 ensures no rotational tipping or rocking instability occurs.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
