BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: A belt drive transmits 15 kW between pulleys running at 20 m/s. If T1 = 2*T2, find tensions and belt cross-section if allowable stress is 2 MPa.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Problem Context & Governing Principles:) Tj
T*
(   This problem investigates the limiting equilibrium and friction mechanics for civil engineering) Tj
T*
(   applications.) Tj
T*
(   Governing criteria involve Coulomb's dry friction law, non-concurrent moment equilibrium,) Tj
T*
(   and normal/tangential coordinate projections at contacting interfaces.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Mathematical Formulation & Step-by-Step Analysis:) Tj
T*
(   Belt Sizing Calculation:) Tj
T*
(   1. Effective Tension: Power P = \(T1 - T2\) * v => 15000 = \(T1 - T2\) * 20 => T1 - T2 = 750 N.) Tj
T*
(   2. Since T1 = 2 * T2: 2 * T2 - T2 = 750 => T2 = 750 N, and T1 = 1500 N.) Tj
T*
ET

